            <div xml:id="d886">

                <pb facs="0741" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/303: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-02T16:00:00+09:00">July 2, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 2—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. Department’s 81, June 12, 4 p.m., American oil claim. Informal and oral
                    representations made today and Consul at Mukden instructed to proceed in
                    accordance with Department’s 64, April 22, 2 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
